# Reference template updates

When `reference/` changes, follow this rule after edits unless the user explicitly says not to sync.

## Live model set

All immediate subdirectories of `tester-v1/configs/` except `reference/`. Discover dynamically; do not hardcode slug names.

## What to sync

Live model directories contain `model.yaml` only (plus optional model-specific experiment variant dirs). **Do not** copy `reference/{variant}/` into live models when reference changes.

After editing `reference/`:

1. **Confirm** each live `{model_slug}/model.yaml` still exists. If a new model slug was added to the repo without `model.yaml`, ask the user for `gguf_path` before writing it (use `reference/model.yaml` as a structural template only).

2. **Do not create or update** `calibration-footprint/`, `calibration-ctx-probe/`, or `hello-world-baseline/` under live models. Calibration and default hello-world runs read those YAML files from `configs/reference/` via `--server` and `--client`.

3. **Do not delete** model-specific variant directories on live models when they are absent from `reference/` (for example `hello-world-bench`).

4. **Do not overwrite** live `{model_slug}/model.yaml` from `reference/model.yaml` when syncing existing models.

## User notification (required)

After reference edits, report explicitly:

- Which files under `reference/` changed.
- That live model dirs were **not** given new variant copies (calibration uses reference indirectly).
- Any live models missing `model.yaml` (if any; ask the user).
- Model-specific dirs on live models were left untouched.

Example:

```text
Updated reference/hello-world-baseline/server.yaml.
Live models: no variant dirs copied (calibration reads configs/reference/).
Preserved: qwen3.5-9b-q8/model.yaml, gemma-4-e4b-it-q8/model.yaml.
Not touched: hello-world-bench on gemma (model-specific).
```
